  not rows. Episodes share days and move together on market-wide news.
  sign: OVER = envelope too wide (actual coverage above nominal), UNDER =
  too narrow. The bracketed count is how many of the 5 levels miss that
  way, so a clean mean cannot hide a mixed pattern.
  far-near carries its own interval because the verdict rests on the
  ORDERING, not on either gap alone, and its WIDTH is what the power screen
  reads to decide whether a cut may vote.

