======================================================================================================================
PRECISION -- which cuts are entitled to vote
======================================================================================================================
  A cut is DECISIVE if the median width of its ten far-minus-near intervals
  is at or under 1.99pp, the effect size from the halves
  analysis. Wider than the effect means the cut cannot resolve it either way.

  cut            near/far rows   median CI width          status
  2025-05-27       1,138/1,569            3.24pp    UNDERPOWERED
  2025-10-24       2,906/3,260            3.32pp    UNDERPOWERED
  2026-03-23       4,610/6,342            2.54pp    UNDERPOWERED
  0 of 3 cuts decisive.

======================================================================================================================
VERDICT ON RECURRENCE
======================================================================================================================
  The rule, stated in the module docstring BEFORE any of the above was run:

  A CELL is (cut, direction, horizon): 3 x 2 x 5 = 30 cells.

  ORDERS      far-half gap > near-half gap (point estimates)
  ORDERS*     the far-minus-near interval excludes zero on the high side
  SIGN SAME   near and far signed bias share a sign
  AS BEFORE   MAE over-covers and MFE under-covers, as at 2026-07-18
  GROWS       the gap at 10h exceeds the gap at 0.5h, per (cut, direction, half)

  A cut is DECISIVE if the median width of its ten far-minus-near intervals is
  at or under the effect being chased (1.99pp, from the halves analysis).
  Wider than that and the cut cannot resolve the effect either way, so it is
  UNDERPOWERED: printed and pooled, but it does not vote on the majority.

  RECURS                requires ALL FOUR of:
                          ORDERS    in >= 70% of all 30 cells
                          ORDERS    in >= 70% of DECISIVE cells
                          SIGN SAME in >= 70% of all 30 cells
                          ORDERS    in >= 7 of 10 cells at a majority of
                                    DECISIVE cuts, and >= 2 decisive cuts exist
  CALENDAR-SPECIFIC     if ORDERS <= 50% of decisive cells (no better than a
                          coin flip) OR the MAE/MFE sign pattern flips between
                          cuts
  UNDERPOWERED          if fewer than 2 cuts are decisive -- the design cannot
                          deliver a majority and no verdict is claimed
  MIXED                 anything else, including pooled and decisive-only
                          tallies landing on opposite sides of 70%. Report as
                          mixed and prefer the simpler fix: periodic refitting
                          on a fixed schedule, no adaptive machinery.

  ALL CELLS
  ORDERS  far gap > near gap            10 of 30     33.3%
  ORDERS* interval excludes zero         0 of 30      0.0%
  SIGN SAME  near and far agree         12 of 30     40.0%
  AS BEFORE  MAE over / MFE under        2 of 30      6.7%
  GROWS  10h gap > 0.5h gap              2 of 12     16.7%

  DECISIVE CELLS ONLY
  none -- every cut's interval is wider than the effect.

  Against coin-flipping, 10 of 30 or better has probability 0.9786. THIS IS NOT A P-VALUE: the 30 cells
  are not independent -- MAE and MFE share episodes and the horizons are
  nested running maxima. It says only how strict the 70% threshold is.

  GROWTH WITH HORIZON -- the other half of the shape. At 2026-07-18 the gap
  barely moved on the near half and more than tripled on the far one:
  near half 0.86 -> 1.29pp, far half 1.35 -> 4.33pp (0.5h to 10h). Quoted, not recomputed.

